{
  "an7.73:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 7.73 ",
  "an7.73:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an7.73:0.3": "About Sunetta ",
  "an7.73:1.1": "“Once upon a time, mendicants, there was a teacher named Sunetta. He was a religious founder and was free of desire for sensual pleasures. ",
  "an7.73:1.2": "He had many hundreds of disciples. ",
  "an7.73:1.3": "He taught them a Dhamma for rebirth in the company of Divinity. ",
  "an7.73:1.4": "Those lacking confidence in Sunetta were—when their body broke up, after death—reborn in a place of loss, a bad place, the underworld, hell. ",
  "an7.73:1.5": "Those full of confidence in Sunetta were—when their body broke up, after death—reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm. ",
  "an7.73:2.1": "Once upon a time, there was a teacher named Mūgapakkha … ",
  "an7.73:2.2": "Aranemi … ",
  "an7.73:2.3": "Kuddālaka … ",
  "an7.73:2.4": "Hatthipāla … ",
  "an7.73:2.5": "Jotipāla … ",
  "an7.73:2.6": "Araka. He was a religious founder and was free of desire for sensual pleasures. ",
  "an7.73:2.7": "He had many hundreds of disciples. ",
  "an7.73:2.8": "He taught them a Dhamma for rebirth in the company of Divinity. ",
  "an7.73:2.9": "Those lacking confidence in Araka were—when their body broke up, after death—reborn in a place of loss, a bad place, the underworld, hell. ",
  "an7.73:2.10": "Those full of confidence in Araka were—when their body broke up, after death—reborn in a good place, a heavenly realm. ",
  "an7.73:3.1": "What do you think, mendi